sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 76/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The script accurately implements the two-regime retino-cortical log-polar map and its exact analytical inverse with the published Bressloff et al. (2001 Section 2; 2002 Eq. 2.1) constants (eps = 0.051, w0 = 0.087, alpha = 3/pi, beta = 1.589/2). It also implements the local orientation harmonics (Eq. 3.12), Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling harmonics (Eq. 4.9), O(beta^2) perturbative dispersion curves (Figs. 16-17), and roll-stability criterion 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0, matching the upstream Rust reference to 2.22e-16. Deduct 10 points because neither the Bressloff (2001 Eq. 3.1) nonlinear integro-differential neural field nor the Rule et al. (2011) periodically forced E-I Floquet system is solved dynamically in Python; planforms are static cosine sums and the Floquet tongues are loaded pre-computed from rule-2011-floquet.json. Deduct 6 points because render_cortical_and_retinal_planform computes retinal polar angle as arctan2(vg, abs(ug)), which restricts theta to [-pi/2, pi/2] (half the 2*pi*beta/eps torus) and forces mirror reflection across the vertical meridian u = 0, destroying spiral chirality. Deduct 5 points because the cubic overlap integrals omit firing-rate nonlinearity derivatives and linear resolvents, eigenfunction harmonics are clamped to [-1.5, 1.5], and quintic terms needed to lift the odd-branch H0/H_pi degeneracy are absent. Deduct 3 points because three of the four gallery panels render a hardcoded preset pattern rather than the branch selected by the cubic amplitude equations. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L95–L120: Exact two-regime log-polar retino-cortical map and analytical inverse with published alpha, beta, eps, w0 constants. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L95-L120>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L423–L507: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling W_n^lat(q), perturbative dispersion branch_growth, and [-1.5, 1.5] harmonic clamping in orientation_eigen_details. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L423-L507>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L810–L865: Static trigonometric planform evaluation bypassing branch selection when pattern != 'auto', and bilateral folding via theta_hemi = np.arctan2(vg, np.abs(ug)). <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L810-L865>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1134–L1145: Rule et al. (2011) Floquet report loaded statically from rule-2011-floquet.json without in-script Floquet integration. <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1134-L1145>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Model fidelity to source' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

